{"school":{"dbn":"17K340","name":"I.S. 340","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"17","district_label":"District 17","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":137,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"227 STERLING PLACE, BROOKLYN, NY 11238","phone":"718-941-5097","website":"www.ms340.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/71786","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"North Star Academy is a small learning community that offers a variety of accelerated and enrichment experiences including advanced courses which result in scholars having the opportunity to take several High School Regents Exams. We integrate technology throughout instruction through the use of Google Suite Education to ensure that our scholars are college and career ready. Every scholar is given access to a laptop to experience the curriculum through an interactive, hands-on, minds-on format. Also, we have a state of the art Science Lab that enables our students to gain hands-on scientific experience. Our extended day learning program offers a variety of enrichment activities (sports, arts, trips, etc.) which allow scholars to learn new skills, gain experiences, and tap into their intellect. Families appreciate the accessibility of administrators and school staff, which helps to build a sense of community that defines our positive school culture. We promote excellence through high expectations of teaching and learning, positive academic behavior, and social and emotional support. We pride ourselves on providing our scholars with a safe, supportive, and highly structured learning environment.","start_time":"08:19am","end_time":"02:39pm","languages":null,"subway":"2, 3 to Grand Army Plaza; B, Q to 7th Av","bus":"B41, B45, B65, B67, B69","shared_building":"1","neighborhood":"Prospect Heights","latitude":40.6762,"longitude":-73.9698,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-2